  "solution": {
    "text": "When $\\mathrm{O}^{-}$changes into $\\mathrm{O}^{2-}$, energy is absorbed i.e the change is endothermic because $\\mathrm{O}^{-}$repels the incoming electron due to similar charge.\nH ice, it needs energy to add (accept) the electron. So, electron affinity $\\left(\\mathrm{EA}_2\\right)$ is positive.",
